      },
      "message": "fix(data): add TRAP_ON_UNIMPLEMENTED_* requirements to Ssstrict\n\nThe Ssstrict extension description states that:\n- \"Attempts to execute unimplemented opcodes... raises an illegal\n  instruction exception\"\n- \"access unimplemented CSRs... raises an illegal instruction exception\"\n\nThis behavior is controlled by the TRAP_ON_UNIMPLEMENTED_INSTRUCTION and\nTRAP_ON_UNIMPLEMENTED_CSR parameters. When Ssstrict is implemented, both\nparameters must be true.\n\nThis commit adds explicit requirements to the Ssstrict extension\ndefinition to enforce this relationship, ensuring that any configuration\nclaiming Ssstrict compliance will have proper trapping behavior for\nunimplemented encodings.\n\nCloses #1319",
